<title>FRANCE: French GDP rose 0.2 pct in fourth quarter 1996.</title>
<headline>French GDP rose 0.2 pct in fourth quarter 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French gross domestic product rose 0.2 percent in the fourth quarter of 1996 after a revised 0.8 percent rise in the third quarter, giving full-year growth of 1.3 percent, national statistics institute INSEE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It originally estimated third quarter growth at 0.9 percent.</p>
<p>It gave the following data (base 1980, changes from previous quarters in percent except stocks variation, in billions of 1980 francs.)</p>
<p>					 Q4	 Q3</p>
<p> Total GDP			   0.2	0.8</p>
<p> Imports			     1.3	2.5</p>
<p> Exports			     1.1	3.6</p>
<p> Household consumption	  -0.5	0.9</p>
<p> Investment			  0.2	0.7</p>
<p> Stocks variation		  1.1     -2.5</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following more detailed breakdown:</p>
<p>				Q4 96  Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95   1996</p>
<p> Total GDP		   0.2    0.8    -0.1   1.2   -0.5     1.3</p>
<p> Imports		     1.3    2.5    -0.4   2.4   -2.7     2.2</p>
<p> Exports		     1.1    3.6    -1.6   4.6   -1.4     3.6</p>
<p> Household consumption  -0.5    0.9    -1.0   2.5   -0.3     2.3</p>
<p> Public consumption	0.4    0.3     0.6   0.3    0.3     1.5</p>
<p> Investment		  0.2    0.7    -0.3  -0.7   -0.3    -0.6</p>
<p>  - business investment -0.1    2.2    -1.0   0.4   -1.5    -0.3</p>
<p>  - household investment 1.1   -2.1     1.6  -1.1    0.1    -0.4</p>
<p>  - public investment    0.0   -0.2    -1.5  -4.6    2.0    -4.3</p>
<p> Stocks variation	  1.1   -2.5     0.3  -7.1    0.2    -8.1</p>
<p> Internal demand	   0.2    0.5     0.2   0.6   -0.9     0.9</p>
<p>INSEE said that the year-on-year growth rate in the last quarter of 1996 was 2.1 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
</text>
